  {
   "id": "step1_col1_deep_departure_scan",
   "description": "cutypen's deep departure-level scan, step 1, TILE COLUMN 1 of 2: the scan climbs through 13 departures and ACCEPTS one: deep convection, cutypen's ktype 1 and the scheme's final ktype 1. Reference: the real64 replay of the chem170 single-column run (em_scm_xy, Weisman-Klemp sounding, dx = 20 km, 59 levels, dt = 60 s, cu_physics = 16) through kernels/ntiedtke_driver of WRF fork branch earthsciml-instrumented-chem170 @ cf3a2bdf, which tapes every departure of the scan (dp_*, one snapshot per departure at the end of its iteration) and cutypen's own outputs (ty_*); the seven cu_ntiedtke_init arguments at binary64, the scheme's literals at their binary32 roundings (FORTRAN_BUGS N109). Inputs: the environment (dp_*), the shallow phase's verdict (sh_ktype, sh_kcbot, sh_kctop, sh_wbase), and each departure's TEACHER TRAJECTORY dp_ptu/dp_pqu/dp_dh (EarthSciAST #701). Algebraic observeds at t = 0 with no ODE state; the empty time_span is one static evaluation. The (departure x level) arrays are compared as Linf errors at 1e-9 of each array's maximum; labels, levels and flags exactly.",
   "inputs": "nt64/1.json",
   "reference": "nt64/1.json",
   "column": 0,
   "time_span": {
    "start": 0,
    "end": 0
   },
   "tolerance": {
    "rel": 1e-09
   },
